WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.778
Every OSINT workflow should start with a clear intelligence requirement:

00:00:03.778 --> 00:00:08.558
the question the work must answer for a named decision or operational need.

00:00:08.558 --> 00:00:12.604
A vague request such as research this company invites uncontrolled searching.

00:00:12.604 --> 00:00:15.546
A useful requirement identifies the subject, timeframe, decision,

00:00:15.546 --> 00:00:17.384
and required level of confidence.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:21.430
Identify who needs the answer and how it will be used.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:25.475
An incident responder may need a rapid assessment within an hour.

00:00:25.475 --> 00:00:30.256
A due-diligence team may accept a longer timeline but require documented primary sources.

00:00:30.256 --> 00:00:33.565
Audience and consequence determine depth, format, review, and escalation.

00:00:33.565 --> 00:00:34.669
Define scope explicitly.

00:00:34.669 --> 00:00:37.611
In-scope elements may include public infrastructure, official records,

00:00:37.611 --> 00:00:40.185
or published statements within a date range.

00:00:40.185 --> 00:00:44.598
Out-of-scope elements may include personal data unrelated to the purpose, private accounts,

00:00:44.598 --> 00:00:49.379
restricted systems, or activity requiring legal authority that the team does not possess.

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:53.056
Record constraints such as deadline, language, geography, approved tools, budget,

00:00:53.056 --> 00:00:54.527
privacy rules, and retention.

00:00:54.527 --> 00:00:57.469
State assumptions and terms that could be ambiguous.

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:01.882
A clear definition of the entity prevents records from different people or

00:01:01.882 --> 00:01:04.457
organizations with similar names from being merged.

00:01:04.457 --> 00:01:07.031
Specify what a satisfactory answer looks like.

00:01:07.031 --> 00:01:10.341
This may include confirmed findings, assessed possibilities, important gaps,

00:01:10.341 --> 00:01:11.444
and recommended validation.

00:01:11.444 --> 00:01:15.857
Set stopping conditions so the team can conclude when the question has

00:01:15.857 --> 00:01:20.270
been answered to the required level or when available public information is

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:20.920
insufficient.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.701
Requirements can change as evidence appears, but changes should be documented and approved.

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:29.378
This preserves accountability and prevents quiet expansion into unrelated collection.

00:01:29.378 --> 00:01:33.423
The requirement remains the anchor for deciding whether each search, source,

00:01:33.423 --> 00:01:34.980
and reported detail is necessary.
